=== part 1b. gauge invariance + all terms at once
    xi -> xi + sigma D maps the pure fold onto a2 = b sigma^2,
    kap = 2 b sigma.  C2 must come back 0.3750 unchanged: a2 enters at
    FIRST order and kap only at SECOND, so this is the sharpest test
    that the two halves of the machine are consistent.
    xidot = a D + b xi^2 + a2 D^2 + kap xi D + b3 xi^3 + be2 xi^2 D + b4 xi^4
    D(t) = eps cos(w t) - eps_qs,  a = b = 1, eps_qs = 0.2
    (eps_qs small so the polynomial keeps its fold structure over the
     whole cycle: |D| <= 2 eps_qs, so the extra terms never dominate aD)
